    "result_text": "Done. The full build is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `membershipTier` is a derived owner field. The codebase already establishes a pattern for these (`householdId`, `membershipNumber`): a tiny self-contained helper class wired in via one `@Mapping` expression. I followed it exactly, which keeps the structural cost minimal \u2014 I didn't grow any existing method or class.\n\n1. **`MembershipTier.java`** (new) \u2014 a small cohesive unit (WMC_other = 0) holding just the rule: `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` and an email is present, else `BRONZE`.\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line on `toOwnerDto` (a low-complexity interface method) delegating to the helper.\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipTier` property so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field in the GET response.\n\n`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` for `AcceptanceTest` (both the SILVER and BRONZE cases) and `BUILD SUCCESS` for the full suite.",
